function analyzeSentence() {
    var sentenceInput = document.getElementById("sentenceInput");
    var sentence = sentenceInput.value;
    var resultContainer = document.getElementById("result");

    if (typeof sentence !== "string") {
        resultContainer.innerHTML = "Error: Input is not a string.";
        return;
    }

    var lowercaseSentence = sentence.toLowerCase();
    var vowelCount = 0;
    var consonantCount = 0;

    for (var i = 0; i < lowercaseSentence.length; i++) {
        var char = lowercaseSentence.charAt(i);
        if (/[aeiou]/.test(char)) {
            vowelCount++;
        } else if (/[a-z]/.test(char)) {
            consonantCount++;
        }
    }

    resultContainer.innerHTML = "Vowels: " + vowelCount + "<br>Consonants: " + consonantCount + "<br>Modified Sentence: " + lowercaseSentence;
}
```

In this example, the HTML code creates a webpage with an input field for the sentence and a button to trigger the analysis. The CSS code styles the webpage for better presentation. The JavaScript code defines a function `analyzeSentence()` that is called when the button is clicked. This function retrieves the sentence input, performs the analysis, and displays the results on the webpage.

