```java
import java.util.Scanner;

class LinkedListSum {
    static class ListNode {
        int val;
        ListNode next;
        ListNode(int x) { val = x; }
    }

    public static ListNode addTwoNumbers(ListNode l1, ListNode l2) {
        ListNode dummyHead = new ListNode(0);
        ListNode p = l1, q = l2, curr = dummyHead;
        int carry = 0;

        while (p != null || q != null) {
            int x = (p != null) ? p.val : 0;
            int y = (q != null) ? q.val : 0;
            int sum = carry + x + y;
            carry = sum / 10;
            curr.next = new ListNode(sum % 10);
            curr = curr.next;
            if (p != null) p = p.next;
            if (q != null) q = q.next;
        }

        if (carry > 0) {
            curr.next = new ListNode(carry);
        }

        return dummyHead.next;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Example input for l1: 2 -> 4 -> 3
        System.out.println("Enter nodes for l1 (separated by space):");
        String[] l1Nodes = scanner.nextLine().split(" ");
        ListNode l1 = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(l1Nodes[0]));
        ListNode current = l1;
        for (int i = 1; i < l1Nodes.length; i++) {
            current.next = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(l1Nodes[i]));
            current = current.next;
        }

        // Example input for l2: 5 -> 6 -> 4
        System.out.println("Enter nodes for l2 (separated by space):");
        String[] l2Nodes = scanner.nextLine().split(" ");
        ListNode l2 = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(l2Nodes[0]));
        current = l2;
        for (int i = 1; i < l2Nodes.length; i++) {
            current.next = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(l2Nodes[i]));
            current = current.next;
        }

        ListNode result = addTwoNumbers(l1, l2);

        // Print the result
        while (result != null) {
            System.out.print(result.val + " ");
            result = result.next;
        }
    }
}
```

This Java program defines a method `addTwoNumbers` that takes two linked lists as input and returns a new linked list representing the sum of the two input lists. The main method reads the input for the two lists from the user, calls the `addTwoNumbers` method, and prints the resulting linked list.

在以下的程式码中，我使用了四个for回圈来生成所有可能的四个数字的组合在一个52张的扑克牌中。扑克牌的表示方式为0-12的数字代表13种花色的A到K，13个数字一个循环代表四种花色。优化方面，我使用了位运算的技巧来减少资源消耗。

```cpp
#include <iostream>
